      "dom_id": "question-6653",
      "name": null,
      "problem": "Which of the following is the graph of $y=-(x-1)^{3}+1?$",
      "worked_solution": "The given function can be obtained by translating $y=-{x}^{3}$ both horizontally and vertically.\n\nWe have two translations:\n\n- the $-1$ inside the parentheses means a horizontal translation of $1$ unit to the *right*, and\n\n- the $+1$ outside the parentheses means a vertical translation of $1$ unit *up*.\n\nSo, the new graph looks as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14226689/assets/2c31f6c2b3f6c9e52d220bdb1c374e47b11d1ca13af0f5fe6cf4a58a06216c80.png)",
